# Cloudflare Pages headers file — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# CAUTION if any Cloudflare zone-level feature ever gets turned on for this
# domain: Rocket Loader and email-address obfuscation both rewrite HTML at
# the edge by injecting their own inline <script> tags. That's compatible
# with script-src below only because 'unsafe-inline' is already there for
# Next's own hydration payload (see the CSP comment) — but if either
# feature is ever enabled, reload a page and check the console for CSP
# violations before assuming it still works.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

# script-src needs 'unsafe-inline' — verified empirically (see the
# CSP-hardening writeup): Next's App Router static export always inlines
# its React Server Components hydration payload as a per-page <script>
# whose content differs on every page and every nightly rebuild, so
# neither a fixed hash list nor a real nonce (no per-request server to
# mint one) is viable without adding a Cloudflare Worker to rewrite every
# response — out of scope for a static-export site today. This does NOT
# cover the inline JSON-LD (Organization/WebSite/Review/BreadcrumbList/
# FAQPage) added elsewhere: those use type="application/ld+json", which
# browsers never treat as executable script, so they're unaffected by
# script-src either way — confirmed with a real CSP + browser test, not
# just docs.

# Server-data shards (public/data/*.json) are rewritten by every nightly
# deploy but keep the same filenames — never let the edge or a browser
# serve last night's snapshot instead of revalidating.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Next content-hashes its own JS/CSS/font chunk filenames, so these are
# safe to cache for as long as a browser will keep them.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
